# Everything here is build output or machine-specific state, and every byte of it
# was being sent to the Docker daemon as build context on each
# `docker compose build`. Without this file the context is ~155MB, of which
# ~151MB is target/ and cpp/build/ -- artefacts compiled for the host, which the
# image must not use and cannot use.
#
# The cost is not only the transfer. A context that changes whenever a local
# `cargo build` runs invalidates the COPY layers on every rebuild, so the image
# recompiles from scratch for reasons that have nothing to do with the source
# having changed.
#
# Note what is NOT here: bench/. It is a workspace member, and cargo refuses to
# load the workspace without its manifest even though nothing in the image builds
# it.

# Build output, both toolchains.
target/
cpp/build/

# Regenerable and machine-specific, and never committed either.
results/

# History and CI config. Neither is read by a build.
.git/
.github/

# The host build config sets -C target-cpu=native, which is exactly wrong for an
# image that may be built and run on different CPUs. The Dockerfile already
# clears RUSTFLAGS; keeping the file out of the context means the setting cannot
# come back by accident.
.cargo/
